<node id="11150446" title="Re^6: Do modules know the callers full path?" created="2023-02-15 17:00:23" updated="2023-02-15 17:00:23" _doctext_mode="lenient"><type id="11">note</type>
<author id="1184095">haj</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;p&gt;Your emphasis &lt;em&gt;&lt;b&gt;the script using the module&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/em&gt; demonstrates the ambiguity of the OP's question.  Is this about the script (which we usually identify as whatever is in &lt;tt&gt;$0&lt;/tt&gt;) or is this the file from which a particular &lt;em&gt;subroutine&lt;/em&gt; was called, as returned by &lt;tt&gt;caller&lt;/tt&gt;?  "Using a module" and "calling a subroutine in a module" are different things and can happen in different files.&lt;/p&gt;</doctext>
